        },
        "doseComparison": {
            "name": "True",
            "status": "unverified"
        },
        "doseComparisonDesc": {
            "name": "The review notes that the amount of hydrogen administered varies by method (e.g., 1.5 L of ~1 mM hydrogen-rich water, inhalation of 2-4% H2 gas), and discusses that higher doses via inhalation may not always be more effective than oral ingestion, suggesting a dose/concentration-dependent effect.",
            "status": "unverified"
        },
        "drugComparison": {
            "name": "True",
            "status": "unverified"
        },
        "comparisonDetail": {
            "name": "The article compares hydrogen therapy to conventional antioxidants and anti-inflammatories, noting that hydrogen selectively reduces excessive oxidative stress and inflammation without impairing beneficial exercise adaptations, unlike traditional supplements which may blunt training benefits.",
